course: dictionary
lesson: 13804
title: Doing things without meaning to
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Involuntarily means without meaning to, without choosing to. Your body does many things involuntarily: your heart beats and you blink without deciding to. «She shivered involuntarily when the cold wind blew.» She did not decide to shiver. Her body did it by itself.
explain: The word can also mean against your will, when someone or something makes you do it. «The sudden loud bang made him jump involuntarily.» Nobody asked him to jump, and he did not choose to. Ask yourself: did the person choose this, or did it just happen?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler phrase, such as "without choosing to". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning. Involuntarily is a long word, but it means the same as "by itself".
fact: Involuntarily means without meaning to or without choosing to.
fact: «Involuntarily» can also mean against your will, when something forces you.
fact: Blinking, sneezing and your heartbeat all happen involuntarily.
fact: «Voluntary» means done by choice, so «involuntary» is its opposite.
fact: «She gasped involuntarily when she saw the spider.» The gasp was a reaction she did not plan.
exercise: «He yawned involuntarily during the long maths lesson.» What does involuntarily mean here? | On purpose, to get attention | With a big smile | Loudly and rudely | *Without meaning to
exercise: Which action happens involuntarily? | *Your heart beating | Choosing to wave at a friend | Reading a book aloud | Writing your name
exercise: Which word in «Her hand jerked involuntarily away from the hot pan.» tells you the jerk was not chosen? | *Involuntarily | Hot | Pan | Hand
test: Sam's eyes watered involuntarily when the onion was cut. What does involuntarily suggest? | Sam was laughing at the onion | Sam had closed his eyes tight | Sam was crying on purpose | *Sam did not choose the watering; it happened by itself
test: «The guard was forced to step aside involuntarily, pushed by the crowd.» What does involuntarily mean? | *Against his will | After a long rest | Happily and with a smile | Quickly, to win a race
exam: «The prince shivered involuntarily as he stepped into the cold dungeon.» Which is the best meaning of involuntarily? | By choice, to show he was brave | Lazily, because he was tired | *Without choosing it, as his body reacted | Very quickly and suddenly on purpose
